Data and ideas from other projects (no code copied):

  Webamp, github.com/captbaritone/webamp
  Copyright (c) 2015 Jordan Eldredge, MIT License.
  The graphic EQ (Geq) uses Webamp's band layout (ten bands, shelves at the
  ends) and the values of Winamp's 17 built-in presets from its
  presets/builtin.json. The .eqf reader is written from the format notes in
  its winamp-eqf package. No Winamp skin or artwork is used. Winamp is a
  trademark of its owner; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  Winamp, Nullsoft or Webamp.

  Winampify, github.com/remigallego/winampify (MIT License)
  The library desktop (Desk), with artists and albums as folders and tracks
  as files, follows its idea.

  awesome-audio-visualization, github.com/willianjusten/awesome-audio-visualization (CC0)
  The Lines, Scope, Spectrogram and Radial label visualizers are ideas found
  through this list, among them its "Lines" experiment and the "Awesome Audio
  Player" and "CircleLineNERDDISCO" pens. They are drawn from scratch on the
  deck's grid.

